<main class="wrapper document-page">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="lead">Agentic Complete is intended as a vendor-neutral capability classification for autonomous systems.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>Purpose</h2>
    <p>
      Technical progress often produces new capability thresholds that require shared language.
      Agentic Complete exists to describe the transition from assisted automation to autonomous continuity.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Neutrality</h2>
    <p>
      The term is implementation-agnostic and vendor-neutral. It does not endorse products, architectures, models, or providers.
      It exists to support clearer evaluation and more consistent discussion.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Scope</h2>
    <p>
      Agentic Complete is not a certification body, not a compliance mark, and not a claim of safety. It is a descriptive standard for discussing autonomous capability.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why Classification Matters</h2>
    <p>
      Useful classifications separate categories that would otherwise be blurred by marketing language.
      Agentic Complete is meant to provide a precise threshold for a specific systems capability: continuous goal-directed operation without human handoffs.
    </p>
  </section>
</main>

